\newlabel{fig:BIG}{{7}{7}{A large map a) corrected by HitL-SLAM b) using human correction, some of which are highlighted c). d) shows an approximate overlay of the map onto an aerial image of the complex from google earth. The map contains over 3000 poses.}{}{}}
\newlabel{fig:LostPoses}{{8}{7}{Initial a) and final b) maps for the `lost poses' experiment. Observations are shown in orange, poses are black arrows, and ground truth (walls) is represented by the black lines. Poses involved in human constraints are colored blue.}{}{}}
\newlabel{fig:small_loop}{{9}{7}{Example of how rank-deficient (collinear) constraints can be combined to effect a full rank constraint. Often, it is easier to tell if two sets of observations are collinear rather than colocated. Supporting rank-deficient constraints allows HitL-SLAM to operate on a larger set of maps.}{}{}}
